.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1000 AM PST Tue Nov 3 2026

Rain showers will continue across the Bay Area and portions of the
Central Coast through late tonight. Temporary reductions in ceiling
height and visibilities are likely as stronger showers roll through.
For now shower chances are likely through 00-06Z before gradually
tapering off overnight. Expect winds to be more southerly during the
day today and gradually becoming more N to NW again by tomorrow
morning.

Vicinity of SFO...Expect showers and temporary reductions in
visibility and ceiling heights through late this evening. Kept CIGs
on the VFR-MVFR border but may see temporary dips lower than in the
TAF. Generally expecting CIGs to rise/fully become VFR by late this
evening as shower chances decrease at SFO. Moderate S to SW winds
continue this morning and will gradually shift more E to NE
overnight before returning to our typical NW flow tomorrow.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Scattered rain showers are expected to move
into Monterey Bay this afternoon, leaving behind lower cloud heights
to linger into the early morning hours. Temporary reductions in
visibility and ceiling heights are likely at MRY and SNS if a
stronger system is able to develop and move onshore. Conditions are
likely to remain MVFR overnight at MRY and SNS.

