.MARINE...
(Today through Sunday)
Issued at 1000 AM PST Tue Nov 3 2026

Moderate to fresh southwesterly breezes will prevail today ahead
of  an approaching cold front. Rain with a low chance for
thunderstorms  are possible this morning and this afternoon,
especially north of  Pigeon Point. Winds will veer to become
northerly Wednesday.  Moderate to rough seas prevail through the
weekend. Drier conditions expected Wednesday into early next week.

&&

.BEACHES...
Issued at 327 AM PST Tue Nov 3 2026

Hazardous beach conditions will be present at
Pacific Coast beaches Tuesday as long period (15-19 second)
northwesterly swell will bring an increased risk for sneaker waves
and strong rip currents. Waves can sweep across the shoreline
without warning, pulling people into the sea from beaches, jetties,
and rocks. Stay off of jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside
infrastructure. Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous surf and
never turn your back on the ocean! Hazardous beach conditions may
linger into Wednesday and thus may warrant an extension of the Beach
Hazards Statement.

